1. “Licensed Premises” refer to any building or part thereof for
which a licence/permit is issued by the relevant authority to carry
out any trade/business as required by the terms of such licence.
2. Premises for which licences are required to carry out trade/
business and for which the police have authority to visit and
inspect books/records are listed hereunder—
(a) Liquor Licences Act, Chap. 84:10, Act No. 3 of 1998
Special Event—
(i) Spirit Retailer’s Licence;
(ii) Wine Retailer’s Licence;
(iii) Hotel Spirit Licence;
(iv) Special Hotel Licence;
(v) Restaurant Licence;
(vi) Special Restaurant Licence;
(vii) Night Bar Licence;
(viii) Spirit Grocer’s Licence;
(ix) Spirit Dealer’s Licence;
(x) Wine Merchant Licence;
(b) Registration of Clubs Act, Chap. 21:01—
(i) Membership Club;
(ii) Proprietary Club;
(iii) Unregistered Club (Chap. 21:01, section 14);
(c) Cinematograph and Video Entertainment Act,
Chap. 20:10—
(i) Cinema
(d) The Gambling and Betting Act, Chap. 11:19—
(i) Racing Pool;
(ii) Common Gambling House;
(e) The Pool Room Act, Chap. 21:02—
(i) Pool  Room;
